WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.267 line:92%
[tense music]

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.002 line:92%
WELL, WELL, WELL...

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.104 line:92%
JACK, WELCOME.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:06.973 line:92%
MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.509
YOU'RE GOING TO BE HERE
FOR QUITE SOME TIME.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.644
- YOU'LL NEVER GET AWAY
WITH THIS, DRAVIC.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:12.712 line:92%
[spits]

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.314 line:92%
- THAT IS ALL, DAQUAN.

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:16.916 line:92%
LEAVE US.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:24.891 line:92%
♪ ♪

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.996
NOW, WHERE WERE WE, THEN?
- [chuckles]

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.697
YOU'RE WASTING
YOUR TIME, DRAVIC.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.633
THE MILITARY CODES
WERE DESTROYED.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.469 line:92%
- IS THAT SO?

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.238 line:92%
I THINK YOU'RE BLUFFING, JACK,

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:41.241 line:92%
AND I AM ABOUT TO CALL...

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.348 line:92%
YOUR BLUFF.

00:00:49.381 --> 00:00:53.319
YOU SEE, JACK,
I AM A PLAYER IN THIS GAME.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:55.121
BUT...
[chuckles]

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.389 line:92%
I'M ALSO THE DEALER.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:59.492
I HOLD ALL OF THE CARDS.
[door rattles]

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:07.967 line:92%
[sighs, clears throat]

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.402 line:92%
[chuckles]

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:12.271
YOU SEE, JACK,
IF I WERE TO GO ALL-IN,

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.407
YOU WOULD NOT BE ABLE
TO COVER THE BET.

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:25.751 line:92%
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

00:01:25.784 --> 00:01:28.221 line:92%
- I WAS THINKING, LIKE,

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.591
MAYBE I COULD BE, LIKE,
YOUR TORTURING ASSISTANT

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.259 line:92%
OR SOMETHING?

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.961
I COULD BE
IN THE ROOM WITH YOU

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.896
AND BE THAT GUY
THAT STANDS IN THE BACKGROUND

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:38.764 line:92%
ALL INTIMIDATING-LIKE.

00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:39.765 line:92%
AND THAT WAY--

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:40.900 line:92%
- FINE, FINE.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.169
OVER THERE,
AND KEEP YOUR TRAP SHUT.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.138
- YEAH, THAT'S WHAT I--
THAT'S WHAT I WAS THINKING.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.477 line:92%
- [chuckles]

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.246
- ARE YOU TWO DONE
WITH YOUR LITTLE LADIES' CHAT?

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.216
- OH!
SHOULDN'T HAVE SAID THAT.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:03.523
- YOU KNOW, JACK, IT'S VERY
APROPOS THAT YOU WOULD SAY THAT,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.659
BECAUSE I FEEL LIKE
WE SHOULD HAVE A CHAT.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:11.331
AND WHEN I SAY "WE,"
I MEAN JUST YOU AND ME.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.336 line:92%
ARE YOU A CHESS PLAYER, JACK?

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:19.005 line:92%
- SURE.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:22.208
- SO THEN YOU ARE AWARE
THAT EACH PIECE

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.376 line:92%
SERVES A DIFFERENT FUNCTION.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.444 line:92%
[plastic crinkling]

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:27.213 line:92%
YOU S--

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.515 line:92%
[crinkling stops]

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:34.120
WHEREAS YOU ARE
MERELY A PAWN,

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.423
YOU SEE, JACK, I AM A QUEEN.
[plastic crinkling]

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:39.625 line:92%
[crinkling stops]

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:43.863
I AM ALLOWED TO MOVE
AROUND THE BOARD WITH IMPUNITY.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.265 line:92%
[plastic crinkling]

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.100 line:92%
WHAT IS WITH THE LOLLIPOP?

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:52.505
- YO, MAN, I WAS THINKING, LIKE,
MAYBE DURING YOUR CHESS SPEECH,

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:53.973
YOU COULD SUCK
ON THIS LOLLIPOP,

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.775
'CAUSE THEN
THAT SHOWS HIM, LIKE,

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.310
YOU SO COMFORTABLE
WITH TORTURE,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:00.279
YOU JUST DO SOMETHING STUPID
LIKE SUCKING ON A LOLLIPOP.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.682 line:92%
YOU SEE WHAT I'M SAYING?

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.817 line:92%
[thud]

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.953
- I NEED YOU TO GO
OVER THERE RIGHT NOW.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.788 line:92%
I NEED YOU TO BE STILL.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.756 line:92%
OKAY?

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:11.991
- OR--
- NO.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:15.628
THERE IS ABSOLUTELY
NO "OR" INVOLVED.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:19.332
GO OVER THERE.
- OKAY.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.933
YOU SHOULDN'T CALL YOURSELF
A QUEEN, THOUGH,

00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:22.235 line:92%
'CAUSE WHERE I'M FROM,

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.703
THAT MEANS SOMETHING DIFFERENT
THAN WHAT--

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.271 line:92%
- SHH.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.340 line:92%
[breathes deeply]

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:31.577 line:92%
JACK...

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.447
I'VE BEEN WAITING
FOR THIS MOMENT

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.384 line:92%
FOR A VERY, VERY LONG TIME.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:41.020
I WANTED TO MAKE
AN INTRODUCTION

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.656 line:92%
TO YOUR NEW BEST FRIEND.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.925 line:92%
[laughs evilly]

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.059 line:92%
- I'LL NEVER TALK.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:50.029
- OH, THIS WILL MAKE
YOU TALK, JACK.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.734
- PLUS, YOU DON'T EVEN
NEED TO STAB HIM AT FIRST.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.670
YOU COULD JUST, LIKE, CARESS
HIS CHEEK WITH THE BLADE--

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:00.072
SOMETHING JUST REAL,
LIKE, CRAZY.

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:02.808
- YEAH, I GOT IT. I GOT IT.
- YEAH, YOU GOOD.

00:04:02.841 --> 00:04:04.443
- THAT'S WHAT
I WAS PLANNING ON DOING.

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:06.345
I'M SORRY.
WHERE DID WE FIND YOU?

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:07.747 line:92%
- SHAQUAN'S COUSIN.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.148 line:92%
- WHO IS SHAQUAN?

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:10.816
- SHAQUAN.
- NO, NO.

00:04:10.849 --> 00:04:12.385 line:92%
I'M ASKING YOU WHO HE IS.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.488
- HE GOT KICKED INTO SOME LAVA,
SO THAT'S WHEN I CAME IN.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.556
- OKAY.
THAT'S WONDERFUL.

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:19.859 line:92%
I NEED YOU TO GO OVER THERE,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.928
AND I NEED YOU TO BE
STOCK-STILL,

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:24.964 line:92%
LIKE A STATUE.

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:27.833
- AH, YEAH, YEAH.
- NOW.

00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:29.869
LIKE, YOU NEED TO
KEEP MOVING IN THAT DIRECTION.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.537
- NO.
YEAH, I'M GOOD.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.538 line:92%
- [sighs]

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.607 line:92%
JACK...

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.776 line:92%
THE MILITARY CODES ARE NOT EVEN

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.779
THE PRIMARY REASON
WHY YOU ARE HERE.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:43.049 line:92%
I WANTED YOU ALL TO MYSELF.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.786
HE'S STANDING BACK THERE
LIKE AN ACTUAL STATUE, ISN'T HE?

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.487 line:92%
- YEAH, IT'S WEIRD.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.424 line:92%
- GOD DAMN HIM.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.293
DAQUAN, YOU DON'T HAVE TO STAND
LIKE AN ACTUAL STATUE--

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:55.995
NOT LITERALLY.
I DIDN'T MEAN IT LITERALLY.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.096 line:92%
- OH, ALL RIGHT.

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.864 line:92%
I THOUGHT THAT SOUNDED STUPID

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:00.199 line:92%
WHEN YOU SAID THAT ORIGINALLY.

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:01.967 line:92%
- YEAH, IT WOULD BE STUPID

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.869
FOR A PERSON
TO DO SOMETHING LIKE THAT.

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.172
- SHOOT, 'CAUSE I DIDN'T KNOW.
I WAS LIKE, "WHAT?

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:07.873 line:92%
THAT DOESN'T MAKE"--

00:05:07.906 --> 00:05:10.509 line:92%
- OKAY.

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.346 line:92%
JACK...

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:18.250
TODAY YOU WILL EXPERIENCE
THE MOST EXQUISITE PAIN.

00:05:18.283 --> 00:05:21.721
I MAY OR MAY NOT--
- OH! YO!

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.556
WE GOT PICTURES
OF HIS GIRLFRIEND.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.990
- UH-HUH.
- THAT'S IT.

00:05:25.023 --> 00:05:26.659
THAT'S PRETTY MUCH TORTURE
OVER RIGHT THERE.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.694
YOU COULD JUST SHOW HIM PICTURES
OF HIS GIRLFRIEND,

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:30.096 line:92%
AND HE'LL DO WHATEVER YOU SAY.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.864
THERE IT IS.
OH!

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:34.200
YOU KNOW WHAT?
EVEN BETTER--WE GOT A CAGE.

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.434 line:92%
IT'S GOT A HOLE AT THE BOTTOM,

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.203
SO YOU COULD PUT THAT
OVER HIS HEAD.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.071
AND THIS OTHER HOLE--
YOU COULD PUT, LIKE,

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:41.173
A RAT OR A SCORPION
UP IN THERE.

00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:43.542
- THAT'S WHAT IT'S THERE FOR,
DAQUAN, ALL RIGHT?

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:46.078
THAT IS WHAT IT IS THERE FOR
IN THE FIRST PLACE.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:48.514
ALL OF THE IMPLEMENTS THAT
YOU'RE SEEING ON THE TABLE THERE

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:51.050
ARE THERE
FOR A PARTICULAR REASON!

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:55.454 line:92%
- WHAT ABOUT THAT?

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:58.290
- OH!
YOU KNOW WHAT?

00:05:58.323 --> 00:06:00.826
DAQUAN, WOULD YOU LIKE
TO BE INVOLVED?

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:04.029
- THAT'S WHAT I WAS THINKING
SINCE THE BEGINNING.

00:06:04.062 --> 00:06:07.433 line:92%
[tense music]

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.335 line:92%
I WAS THINKING...

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:13.101
MAYBE YOU SHOULD JUST TELL HIM,
LIKE, THE MILITARY CODES.

